WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.875
A handful of other rules that catch charter captains.

2
00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:05.600
Your wake.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.825
You’re legally responsible for it, and for any damage or injury it causes.

4
00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:15.025
Slow down near docks, small boats and anchored vessels.

5
00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:17.150
Naval vessels.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.475
Within five hundred yards of a large American naval vessel, you operate at minimum speed.

7
00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:27.575
And you may not come within one hundred yards without permission.

8
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:29.725
Five hundred, slow.

9
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:32.100
One hundred, stay out.

10
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:38.725
Many Florida ports enforce security zones around cruise ships, tankers and port facilities.

11
00:00:38.975 --> 00:00:43.750
Florida law covers boating under the influence and reckless operation.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.725
And remember your own limit as a commercial operator.

13
00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:49.475
What was it?

14
00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:52.450
Zero point zero four.

15
00:00:52.700 --> 00:01:01.475
And when the Coast Guard or the Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission signals you to stop for a boarding, comply promptly and politely.
